[0.000, "o", "         \"managedFields\": [\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "           {\r\n"]
[0.011, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mpropose_manifestwork\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mThe agent PROPOSES a change. It must pass static guardrails and a Kyverno dry-run first; nothing is applied yet.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: propose_manifestwork\u001b[0m\r\n     proposal_id=4ad043eaa13a4d5d807faeda5b9c2cc0\r\n     status=pending_approval\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[PASS]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mapply with a BAD token\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mProve the gate holds: apply with an invalid token must be refused by the server, not applied.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: apply_manifestwork(bad token)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     REJECTED: Malformed approval token.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mocm-mcp approve (human)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA human on a trusted terminal mints an approval token: an Ed25519 signature binding the exact content and operation. The server holds only the public key, so it can verify a token but can never mint one - and neither can the agent.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ ocm-mcp approve 4ad043eaa13a4d5d807faeda5b9c2cc0\u001b[0m\r\n     token minted (...hMIhWR0CeKAQ)\r\n"]
[0.006, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mapply_manifestwork(token)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mWith a valid token, the server verifies it and delivers the change as an OCM ManifestWork.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: apply_manifestwork\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n       \"status\": \"applied\",\r\n       \"cluster\": \"cluster1\",\r\n       \"manifestwork\": \"e2e-demo\",\r\n       \"note\": \"Verify rollout with get_cluster_health / get_manifestwork. To undo, call propose_rollback then apply the rollback with a fresh approval.\"\r\n     }\r\n"]
[5.005, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[PASS]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mget_manifestwork (verify)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mConfirm the hub actually applied it on the spoke.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: get_manifestwork\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n       \"cluster\": \"cluster1\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "       \"name\": \"e2e-demo\",\r\n       \"conditions\": {\r\n         \"Applied\": \"True\",\r\n         \"Available\": \"True\"\r\n       },\r\n       \"resources\": [\r\n         {\r\n           \"resource\": \"ConfigMap/ocm-mcp-e2e\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "           \"namespace\": \"shop\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "           \"conditions\": {\r\n"]
[0.012, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mpropose_cluster_action(cordon)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mPropose adding a NoSelect taint so Placements stop scheduling here - still gated by approval.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: propose_cluster_action\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n       \"proposal_id\": \"5ca137d378a34124be31e6af914a9645\",\r\n       \"status\": \"pending_approval\",\r\n       \"action\": \"cordon\",\r\n       \"next_step\": \"Ask the human operator to run: ocm-mcp approve 5ca137d378a34124be31e6af914a9645 and provide you the approval token, then call apply_cluster_action.\"\r\n     }\r\n"]
[0.016, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mapply_cluster_action(cordon)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mApplied after approval; the taint now keeps new work off this cluster.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: apply_cluster_action\u001b[0m\r\n     taints=[{\"effect\": \"NoSelect\", \"key\": \"ocm-mcp-server.io/cordoned\", \"timeAdded\": \"2026-07-28T02:23:29Z\", \"value\": \"true\"}]\r\n"]
[0.029, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36muncordon (restore)\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mRemove the taint so the cluster is schedulable again.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: apply_cluster_action(uncordon)\u001b[0m\r\n     taints_after=[]\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mprompt: diagnose_fleet\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA ready-made, safety-first runbook an agent can start from.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ mcp prompt: diagnose_fleet\u001b[0m\r\n     You are operating a Kubernetes fleet through the OCM hub. Investigate only - do not propose or apply anything yet.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     \r\n     1. Call list_clusters to see availability, version, and capacity of every cluster.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     2. Call get_addon_health to spot Degraded or unavailable add-ons across the fleet.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     3. For any cluster that is Unavailable or not joined, call get_cluster to read its conditions, then get_cluster_health for unhealthy pods and degraded deployments.\r\n     4. For each unhealthy workload, use query_events and get_pod_logs to find the cause.\r\n     5. Produce a concise report: per cluster, what is wrong, the evidence, and the smallest safe remediation you would propose. Do not act on it yet.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mprompt: remediate_with_approval\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA ready-made, safety-first runbook an agent can start from.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ mcp prompt: remediate_with_approval\u001b[0m\r\n     A fleet operator reports: payments degraded on cluster1\r\n     \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     Follow the safe remediation workflow:\r\n     1. Investigate with the read tools (list_clusters, get_cluster_health, query_events, get_pod_logs, get_manifestwork) until you can name the root cause with evidence.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     2. Decide the smallest change that fixes it. For a workload change, call propose_manifestwork with pinned images and a precise summary. For a cluster lifecycle change (cordon, uncordon, set a label, accept a cluster), call propose_cluster_action.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     3. If the proposal is REJECTED by static guardrails or Kyverno, read the reason, correct the manifest, and propose again. Never try to bypass a rejection.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     4. Tell the operator the proposal id and ask them to run `ocm-mcp approve <id>` and give you the token. Wait for it.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     5. Call the matching apply tool with the token. Then verify recovery with reads.\r\n     6. Finish by calling get_audit_trail an\r\n     ... (truncated)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mprompt: why_not_scheduled\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mA ready-made, safety-first runbook an agent can start from.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ mcp prompt: why_not_scheduled\u001b[0m\r\n     Explain why cluster 'cluster1' was or was not selected by Placement 'demo-all' in namespace 'default'. Use only reads:\r\n     \r\n     1. get_placement_decision('demo-all', 'default') for the clusters actually chosen.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     2. list_placements to read the Placement's clusterSets and selection intent.\r\n     3. get_cluster('cluster1') for its labels, ClusterClaims, and taints.\r\n     4. list_cluster_set_bindings to confirm the Placement's namespace is bound to the ClusterSet the cluster belongs to.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     5. list_addon_placement_scores('cluster1') if the Placement uses AddOn prioritizers.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     6. Conclude with the specific reason: not in a bound ClusterSet, failed a predicate, carries a NoSelect taint, or simply out-scored by others.\r\n"]
[0.008, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mlist_pending_proposals\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mProposals still awaiting human approval.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: list_pending_proposals\u001b[0m\r\n     [\r\n       {\r\n         \"id\": \"b5f924e6d7b4461cb049fc7d264fc059\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "         \"cluster\": \"cluster1\",\r\n         \"kind\": \"action\",\r\n         \"action\": \"uncordon\",\r\n         \"name\": \"uncordon-cluster1\",\r\n         \"summary\": \"Undo.\"\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "       },\r\n       {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "         \"id\": \"b84e8f66ab8b4a4a9dc271f006674511\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "         \"cluster\": \"cluster1\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mget_audit_trail\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mThe append-only log of every tool call so far - the agent writes its incident report from this record, not from memory.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: get_audit_trail\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     [\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     {\"tool\": \"apply_manifestwork\", \"args\": {\"proposal_id\": \"4ad043eaa13a4d5d807faeda5b9c2cc0\", \"approval_token\": \"<redacted>\"}, \"outcome\": \"rejected\", \"error\": \"\", \"duration_ms\": 0, \"ts\": 1785205404.866405, \"actor\": \"sandeepbazar:17013\", \"seq\": 31, \"prev\": \"136a919eaa5b57646e57381d236adc0ec7460db79470344c9266c81fdae197b4\", \"hash\": \"ade2fac476383e42a5f084a1ea5b4f00cc562f6c5f44f439204909a83bc9ab01\"},\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     {\"tool\": \"apply_manifestwork\", \"args\": {\"proposal_id\": \"4ad043eaa13a4d5d807faeda5b9c2cc0\", \"approval_token\": \"<redacted>\"}, \"outcome\": \"ok\", \"error\": \"\", \"duration_ms\": 5, \"ts\": 1785205404.872483, \"actor\": \"sandeepbazar:17013\", \"seq\": 32, \"prev\": \"ade2fac476383e42a5f084a1ea5b4f00cc562f6c5f44f439204909a83bc9ab01\", \"hash\": \"e403a015b9085ac199080eddbd462295dddbf9da99645645013501695ae744fd\"},\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     {\"tool\": \"get_manifestwork\", \"args\": {\"cluster\": \"cluster1\", \"name\": \"e2e-demo\"}, \"outcome\": \"ok\", \"error\": \"\", \"duration_ms\": 3, \"ts\": 1785205409.8769238, \"actor\": \"sandeepbazar:17013\", \"seq\": 33, \"prev\": \"e403a015b9085ac199080eddbd462295dddbf9da99645645013501695ae744fd\", \"hash\": \"d5ac8dc58aae705357ff37d41852cf06120ece0289df2405a63ba9c587b5d78b\"},\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     {\"tool\": \"propose_cluster_action\", \"args\": {\"cluster\": \"cluster1\", \"action\": \"cordon\", \"summary\": \"Cordon for maintenance.\", \"params_json\": \"{}\"}, \"outcome\": \"ok\", \"error\": \"\", \"duration_ms\": 11, \"ts\": 1785205409.889554, \"actor\": \"sandeepbazar:17013\", \"seq\"\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     ... (truncated)\r\n"]
[0.096, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;35m[INJECT]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mINJECT: failing-rollout\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mDeploy a 'payments-v2' with a broken image tag, exactly the kind of bad rollout that pages someone at 2 a.m.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ ./chaos/inject.sh failing-rollout cluster1\u001b[0m\r\n     deployment.apps/payments-v2 created\r\n     injected: failing-rollout into cluster1\r\n"]
[12.019, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mDIAGNOSE: get_cluster_health\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mThe agent asks 'what is unhealthy here?' and sees payments-v2 is not running.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: get_cluster_health(cluster1)\u001b[0m\r\n     {\r\n       \"unhealthy_pods\": [\r\n         {\r\n           \"namespace\": \"shop\",\r\n           \"name\": \"payments-v2-6f6596d897-5jb74\",\r\n           \"phase\": \"Pending\",\r\n           \"waiting\": [\r\n             \"ErrImagePull\"\r\n           ],\r\n           \"restarts\": 0\r\n         },\r\n         {\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[OK]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mDIAGNOSE: query_events\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mEvents reveal the root cause in plain English: the image cannot be pulled.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: query_events(cluster1, shop)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     [\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "       {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "         \"namespace\": \"shop\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "         \"type\": \"Normal\",\r\n         \"reason\": \"BackOff\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "         \"object\": \"Pod/payments-v2-6f6596d897-5jb74\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "         \"count\": 1,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "         \"message\": \"Back-off pulling image \\\"registry.k8s.io/e2e-test-images/agnhost:2.47-nonexistent\\\"\"\r\n       },\r\n       {\r\n         \"namespace\": \"shop\",\r\n         \"type\": \"Warning\",\r\n"]
[0.006, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m[FIX]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mFIX: propose + approve\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mThe agent proposes the smallest safe fix (a pinned, known-good image). It clears the guardrails and a human approves it.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ propose_manifestwork -> ocm-mcp approve\u001b[0m\r\n     proposal_id=cc20be03b30a446fa6e279e804025825\r\n     guardrails=passed  kyverno_dry_run=passed  approved=yes\r\n"]
[0.006, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m[FIX]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mFIX: apply_manifestwork\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mDelivered to the cluster through the hub as a ManifestWork.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: apply_manifestwork(token)\u001b[0m\r\n     status=applied\r\n"]
[6.018, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32m[PASS]\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36mVERIFY: recovery\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90mRe-read health until payments-v2 is running again - the incident is closed, with a full audit trail of everything that happened.\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[0;90m$ tool: get_cluster_health(cluster1)\u001b[0m\r\n     payments-v2 is Running again - fix confirmed end to end.\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32me2e_tools.py finished (0 failures).\u001b[0m\r\n"]
